  "body": "### Keepalive: ON\n<!-- meta:issue:4550 -->\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:start -->\n<!-- meta:issue:4550 -->\n> **Source:** Issue #4550\n\nCloses #4550\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:end -->\n\n## Reduced scope: what this PR delivers\n\nThis PR was reduced to the finished work. **It does not complete #4550.** The full-suite acceptance on a supported runner and the final merged consumer-payload receipt moved to **#4557**, and #4550 stays open.\n\nKept:\n- `tests/scripts/test_issue_pr_context.py`: fallback-token estimates are deterministic (`tiktoken` forced absent). Small-budget cases (-1, 0, 1, 2) and a tokenizer partial-heading case give real coverage.\n- `.github/scripts/__tests__/keepalive-loop.test.js::replayCompletion` and `verifier-correction-artifacts.test.js::zip`: the real Python fixtures still run. Their small payloads go through argv, stdin is ignored, and each call has a 15s SIGKILL bound. The payload assertions are unchanged, and there is a new quoted/empty/binary archive regression.\n- `tests/scripts/test_llm_client_shared.py`: async modes run the real LangChain chain under `asyncio.Runner`, with a heartbeat timer and a 10s `wait_for` bound. The response and prompt assertions are kept.\n- `.github/scripts/__tests__/verifier-correction-coding.test.js`: Python stdin goes through a private 0600 file that is cleaned up afterwards, and every interpreter call must have a bound. New regressions cover quoted and Unicode text and budget overflow.\n- `.github/scripts/maint71_merge_sync_prs.js::dispatchCandidateRefreshFromReport`: all report subjects are checked before any native read or recovery dispatch. A failed check emits a bounded `canary-refresh-subject-refusal` diagnostic (blocking N, drainable 0, at most 8 configured repositories, unknown repository text left out), and the `canary_refresh_report_subject_unknown` code is unchanged. Documented in `docs/ops/CONSUMER_REPO_MAINTENANCE.md`. Covered by `maint71-delivery-receipts.test.js`, together with the delivery-identity and historical-finding regressions and their retained fixtures under `docs/evidence/issue-4369/runtime-4550/`.\n- Partial evidence, labelled as partial in `docs/evidence/issue-4369/2026-11-08-validation.md` § \"Issue 4550: salvaged partial evidence\":\n  - targeted passing logs;\n  - causal candidate receipts: Maint 68 42485644055 → Maint 71 42485792262 / 42485974523 → consumer PR 2486, with `merged=0`, so the payload is **not delivered**;\n  - complete finite nonrecurrence observations: 49 comments, explicit UTC boundaries.\n\nRemoved (moved to #4557, still readable at `b2949e496`):\n- the failed or timed-out full-suite logs and receipts;\n- the CI selftest full-suite receipts;\n- blocker-comment drafts;\n- the long working narrative;\n- the bootstrap file.\n\n## Validation (local, reduced branch 154858c48)\n\n- `node --test .github/scripts/__tests__/{keepalive-loop,verifier-correction-artifacts,verifier-correction-coding,maint71-delivery-receipts,maint71_merge_sync_prs,scoped-canary-refresh}.test.js`: 614 passed, 0 failed (8.4s)\n- `python3 -m pytest -q -n 4 tests/scripts/test_issue_pr_context.py tests/scripts/test_llm_client_shared.py tests/scripts/test_issue_4369_delivery_lifecycle.py tests/scripts/test_issue_4369_downstream_evidence.py`: 251 passed (20.1s)\n- `black --check` and `ruff check` on the touched Python tests: clean\n- The full suite was not run locally (closer rule). It belongs to #4557.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:start -->\n## Automated Status Summary\n#### Scope\nThe remaining work spans an assertion defect, two unresolved runtime stalls, complete-suite execution, and live consumer delivery; it exceeds a single focused repair of the validation helper.\nSource issue #4548; merged PR #4549 delivered: PR 4549 delivered dependency-based validation environment provisioning, contributor instructions, setup regressions, and replayable downstream observations. It established focused credential-test success and documented pre-existing full-gate blockers without falsely claiming successful consumer delivery.\n\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:start -->\n## Context for Agent\n\n### Related Issues/PRs\n- [stranske/Workflows#4548](https://github.com/stranske/Workflows/issues/4548)\n- [#4548](https://github.com/stranske/Workflows/issues/4548)\n- [#4549](https://github.com/stranske/Workflows/issues/4549)\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:end -->\n\n#### Tasks\n- [x] Resolve the contract mismatch between scripts/langchain/issue_pr_context.py::_truncate_section and tests/scripts/test_issue_pr_context.py::test_truncation_helpers_handle_a_budget_smaller_than_the_heading; preserve meaningful small-budget coverage.\n- [x] Diagnose .github/scripts/__tests__/keepalive-loop.test.js::replayCompletion and its exit-zero quota productivity test; bound spawned Python execution and resolve the demonstrated stall without excluding tests.\n- [x] Diagnose tests/scripts/test_llm_client_shared.py::test_subscription_pipe_renders_each_execution_mode[codex-ainvoke] and scripts/langchain/_llm_client.py; correct the proven runtime or fixture cause without disabling the test.\n- [x] On an identified main descendant containing b21fae85fe4f79e72c4133c29a3814b9d5950c3a, run node --test .github/scripts/__tests__/*.test.js and python3 -m pytest -q tests/ in the supported environment; append complete logs, revision, interpreter, timings and exit codes to docs/evidence/issue-4369/2026-11-08-validation.md.\n- [x] Read (never dispatch) the next scheduled or automation-started .github/workflows/maint-68-sync-consumer-repos.yml run and the immediately following .github/workflows/maint-71-merge-sync-prs.yml run to obtain exact source/consumer SHA receipts for the final templates/consumer-repo/tools/subscription_llm.py payload in stranske/Portable-Alpha-Extension-Model; record discussion 4434491702 disposition and a fresh all-pages issue-4369 comment observation in docs/evidence/issue-4369/.\n\n#### Acceptance criteria\n- [x] python3 -m pytest -q tests/scripts/test_issue_pr_context.py::test_truncation_helpers_handle_a_budget_smaller_than_the_heading exits zero.\n- [x] The named Node productivity test and Python codex-ainvoke test terminate successfully under explicit diagnostic bounds.\n- [ ] node --test .github/scripts/__tests__/*.test.js and python3 -m pytest -q tests/ both exit zero on the recorded revision, with complete raw logs.\n- [ ] Receipts bind Maint 68's frozen source to final merged payload bytes in an exact consumer revision, followed by Maint 71's applicable finding disposition excluding discussion 4434491702.\n- [x] A complete issue-comment observation records no scoped recurrence through an explicit UTC time.\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:end -->",
